## Dialog action buttons (mandatory)

### Mobile spacing

- Use `gap-3` for vertical stacking on mobile, `sm:gap-2` for horizontal on desktop.
- Pattern: `className="flex flex-col gap-3 pt-4 sm:flex-row sm:gap-2"`

### Destructive actions require confirmation

- **Delete** actions must show a confirmation dialog before executing.
- Use a state variable (e.g., `showDeleteUserConfirm`) to control the confirmation dialog.

### Primary/CTA buttons

- The primary action button (Save, Confirm, Submit) must use `variant="default"` or `variant="brand"`.
- Secondary actions (Cancel) use `variant="outline"`.
- Destructive actions use `variant="destructive"`.

### Confirmation dialog button order

- Cancel button comes first (left on desktop, top on mobile).
- Destructive/confirm action comes last (right on desktop, bottom on mobile).
- Use `sm:justify-end` to align buttons to the right on desktop.

### Example:

```tsx
<div className="flex flex-col gap-3 pt-4 sm:flex-row sm:justify-end sm:gap-2">
	<Button
		variant="outline"
		onClick={() => setShowDeleteUserConfirm(false)}
		className="gap-2"
	>
		<X size={16} />
		Cancel
	</Button>
	<Button variant="destructive" onClick={handleDeleteUser} className="gap-2">
		<Trash2 size={16} />
		Delete
	</Button>
</div>
```
